course: dictionary
lesson: 2854
title: A word for a dog
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: "Doggie" is a child's word for a dog, often a small or cute one. Grown-ups use it in baby talk and picture books, as in «Look at that nice doggie!» The word is friendly and loving, so the context tells you how it feels.
explain: Doggie has two other meanings. A doggy bag is a bag for taking home food you did not finish at a restaurant. Doggy paddle is a simple way of swimming, paddling with your hands like a dog, and it is often the first stroke children learn.
explain: Doggie and doggy are two spellings of the same word. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: a dog in the park, a bag at a restaurant, or a stroke in the pool. If you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Doggie is a child's word for a dog, especially a small or cute one.
fact: A doggy bag is a bag for taking home food you did not finish at a restaurant.
fact: Doggy paddle is a simple swimming stroke, paddling with your hands like a dog.
fact: Doggie and doggy are two spellings of the same word.
fact: «Tsutsyk» means puppy or doggie and is a loving word.
exercise: «Look at that cute doggie wagging its tail!» What does doggie mean? | A bag for food | *A dog, often a small or cute one | A kind of swimming stroke | A type of cake
exercise: After dinner Mum asks for a doggy bag. What is a doggy bag? | A bag for walking a dog | *A bag for taking home food you did not finish | A bag full of toys | A swimming bag for the pool
exercise: At swimming lessons Ella learns to paddle with her hands like a dog. What is this stroke called? | Butterfly | *Doggy paddle | Backstroke | Front crawl
test: In the sentence «tsutsyk» means puppy or doggie and is a loving word. What does «tsutsyk» mean? | *Puppy or doggie | A swimming stroke | A type of food | A loud noise
test: Which phrase means a bag for leftover food from a restaurant? | *Doggy bag | Nice doggie | Doggy paddle | Dog walker
exam: A swimming teacher says, «Try the doggy paddle.» What does she mean? | A bag for leftovers from dinner | A small dog that is very cute | *A way of swimming, paddling with your hands like a dog | Lying still and floating on your back
